{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall place in the Ark.</b> In it the fragments of the tablets were always kept, and those they would take to war, as is taught in the Sifrei: ״וארון ברית ה׳ נוסע לפניהם״ — this one that went out with them in the camps was the wooden ark that Moses made when he went up to Sinai, and at first he placed in it the fragments of the tablets and also the second tablets, as it is written: ״ואשים את הלוחות בארון אשר עשיתי״ — until the golden ark that Bezalel made was made. And when it was made, they placed the second tablets in it, as it is said: ״ונתת אל הארון את העדות אשר אתן אליך״. And that one which Bezalel made they were not accustomed to take to war, as it is written in the battle of Eben-ha-Ezer: ״מי יצילנו מיד האלהים האדירים האלה״ — ״כי לא היתה כזאת מתמול שלשום״, because they were not accustomed to take it, and there they were struck and the ark was captured. And regarding the ark that Bezalel made, this is what the Rabbis said: as long as the ark and the Shekhinah are not in their place, Israel are forbidden in marital relations. And that which is written concerning Uriah, who said: ״הארון וישראל חנים בסוכות ואני אלך לשכב עם אשתי״ — this implies that he was stringent upon himself, but the others are permitted in marital relations — that is regarding the wooden ark that Moses made, which they would take to war. And what happened in the battle of Joshua, that it went with them — that was by divine decree. And that which we say at the end of the first chapter of Bava Batra: this teaches that the tablets and the fragments of the tablets were kept in the ark — and the implication there is that this is the ark Bezalel made — that is in the structure where there was ״מנוחה עדי עד״. And in the Yerushalmi there is a dispute: some say there was one ark, and some say two arks."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:49.233596811Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}